# Per-Dockerfile ignore (BuildKit honors <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the
# context-root .dockerignore). The UI image builds from the REPO ROOT to reach
# the shared wording vector, so this trims the root context to what the Vite
# build needs -- the UI sources + lockfile and that one vector stay; everything
# else (the Python trees, the Rust CLI, the runner, docs, other packages,
# installed deps and build output) is dropped.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
apps/ui/dist
apps/ui/test-results
apps/ui/playwright-report
apps/ui/.vite
apps/api
apps/dispatcher
apps/worker
runner
cli
docs
prototypes
charts
otel
scripts
tests/*
!tests/vectors
tests/vectors/*
!tests/vectors/user-action-wording.json
packages
*.md
**/*.md
**/.env
